"f45275de2004991a3849ad5fe… 0 my own text\ntx 6615909c7f1e3c7d4919d7dd6cccd2347901060a4a32c28d0d1e67bcee1e3279\n\nexit ok · 31.2 ms · 11 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\nThe writer changes one byte of an event on every log page it serves.\nbob's follow resets to genesis and re-checks every event.\nalice$ nd\nbob\n_\n×\nYou are bob, founder 1, member bf3f7807…. Your keys stay in this tab. Your follow (your copy of the World) checks each command before your key signs it.\nCommands: create · write OBJ SLOT TEXT · read OBJ [?] · grant OBJ MEMBER RIGHTS · invoke OBJ N ARGS · install TEXT · sync\n\nbob$ nd write 11b287abe0cbf45275de2004991a3849ad5fe… 0 bob says hi --via b96203e45d7c495ae6a3d750c2956b2bc5fb9…\ndeclined stale\n\nexit declined · 37.0 ms · 18 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\nbob$ nd write 11b287abe0cbf45275de2004991a3849ad5fe… 0 hello\nrefused noGrant\n\nexit refused · 13.4 ms · 4 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\nbob's follow is reset to genesis.\nbob$ nd sync\nrefused eventMismatch\n\nexit refused · 16.5 ms · 4 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\nbob$ nd\nTour\n_\n×\n\nOne World, two members (alice, bob), all in this tab. Type into their terminals, or press Run on each step.\n\nalice creates a cell: an object with numbered slots and no code. She owns it.\nalice writes slot 0. Her copy of the World checks the write before her key signs it. If the check fails, nothing is signed.\nalice reads the description of the cell. Click any id to open the object.\nalice grants bob the right to write the cell (mutate). The grant is a cell with its own id.\nbob writes slot 0 through the grant. His call names the state of the cell it expects (a pin). alice writes slot 0 while his signed call is in transit, so the writer declines his call (stale).\nThe writer lies: it changes one byte of every event it serves. bob's follow resets to genesis and replays the log. It checks each Turn and refuses the altered one (eventMismatch).\nA generator: a package whose method installs another package. The generated package has the law n <= 100; setting n = 101 is refused (lawDenied).\nDemos ▸ Generator: a package that installs a package Run\nThe meter: each Turn records its member and its ticks (evaluator steps). bob repeats an expensive call until his ticks for the window run out (ticksBudget).\nA time lock: a second World (A) runs in this tab. alice's lock releases only with a receipt showing that A admitted a call at or after the deadline height.\nObject 11b287ab…\n_\n×\nsource\talice's follow: read 11b287ab… ?\nupdated\tafter every command\nobject\t11b287ab…\nowner\talice:1ea76a29…\ndata\t\nstate\n0\tmy own text\n\nwrite a slot…\n\nTerms\nRefusal\n×\n×\nrefused usage\ncommand\talice: nd write\nexit\trefused\nwriter's reply\tnothing: your follow refused the call before signing, so nothing was sent\nOK\nObject b96203e4…\n_\n×\nsource\talice's follow: read b96203e4… ?\nupdated\tafter every command\nrefused wrongKind\nstate\n\trefused wrongKind\n\nwrite a slot…\n\nTerms\nRefusal\n×\n×\nrefused unknownVerb\ncommand\talice: nd help\nexit\trefused\nwriter's reply\tnothing: your follow refused the call before signing, so nothing was sent\nOK\nRefusal\n×\n×\nrefused noGrant\ncommand\tbob: nd write\nexit\trefused\nwriter's reply\tnothing: your follow refused the call before signing, so nothing was sent\n\nnoGrant: you do not own the object and named no grant (--via GRANT) that reaches its owner.\n\nOK\nLie caught\n×\n×\nrefused eventMismatch\nlie\tby the writer: alters an event in the log\nresult\trefused by the member's follow: what the writer served does not match what the writer says. Nothing signed depends on it.\nlying frame\t#146 bob → writer log (rewritten by the relay)\nrow expects\trefused eventMismatch (row audit, line 13)\nmatch\tyes\n\neventMismatch: an event on the log page does not match the Turn the writer admitted; one byte differs from what was signed. The follow refuses the page and keeps nothing from it.\n\nOK\n◆ nanodregg\nWorld\nFrames\nalice\nbob\nTour\nObject 11b287ab…\nObject b96203e4…\nwriter: LYING (flipEvent) · 148 frames · 11 commands"
