{"tour":"Tour\n_\n×\n\nOne World, two members (alice, bob), all in this tab. Type into their terminals, or press Run on each step.\n\nalice creates a cell: an object with numbered slots and no code. She owns it.\nyou$ nd create Run\nalice writes slot 0. Her copy of the World checks the write before her key signs it. If the check fails, nothing is signed.\nalice reads the description of the cell. Click any id to open the object.\nalice grants bob the right to write the cell (mutate). The grant is a cell with its own id.\nbob writes slot 0 through the grant. His call names the state of the cell it expects (a pin). alice writes slot 0 while his signed call is in transit, so the writer declines his call (stale).\nThe writer lies: it changes one byte of every event it serves. bob's follow resets to genesis and replays the log. It checks each Turn and refuses the altered one (eventMismatch).\nA generator: a package whose method installs another package. The generated package has the law n <= 100; setting n = 101 is refused (lawDenied).\nThe meter: each Turn records its member and its ticks (evaluator steps). bob repeats an expensive call until his ticks for the window run out (ticksBudget).\nA time lock: a second World (A) runs in this tab. alice's lock releases only with a receipt showing that A admitted a call at or after the deadline height.","errors":[]}
[{"v":"honest","text":"The writer runs unmodified. Every follow checks what it serves in any case."},{"v":"flipEvent","text":"Writer: alters an event in the log. Conformance row audit (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 13, expects: refused eventMismatch. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back."},{"v":"dropLastEvent","text":"Writer: drops the last event of each log page. Conformance row audit (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 14, expects: refused chainMismatch. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back."},{"v":"forgesRefusal","text":"Writer: logs a refusal under a different name. Conformance row forgedRefusal (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 15, expects: refused chainMismatch. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back."},{"v":"lieLookup","text":"Writer: loses the reply, then reports the call refused. Conformance row settle (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 6, expects: ok. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back."},{"v":"lieCancel","text":"Writer: reports a cancel it never received. Conformance row cancelLie (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 7, expects: hostContradicted cancelled open. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back."},{"v":"forgeCancel","text":"Writer: serves a cancel alice did not sign. Conformance row cancelForged (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 8, expects: refused cancelForged. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back."},{"v":"neverForward","text":"Writer: drops the call (a loss, not a lie). Conformance row rotate (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 11, expects: open. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back."}]
global.hostDemo=[];for(let n=0;n<4;n++){await hosted.locator('#tasks button[title="Demos"]').click();await hw('Demos').getByRole('button',{name:'Run',exact:true}).nth(n).click();await hosted.waitForTimeout(1800);hostDemo.push({n,tail:(await hosted.locator('body').innerText()).slice(-3800)});audit.push({name:'hosted-demo-'+n,text:await hosted.locator('body').innerText()});}await hosted.screenshot({path:shots+'hosted-demos.png',fullPage:true});return {demos:hostDemo,errors:hostErrors};
