"52 this window\nalice$ nd invoke d5223e85a22005ae70ca83fac51176397dd4e… 0 (record (n 50))\ntx b8cf0f4f6a78bc7c96d2085995d1a904e6f23977bdca372f27632fb60e40239a\n\nexit ok · 56.8 ms · 19 frames · ticks 1,580 / 2,097,152 this window\nalice sets n = 101. The law refuses it (lawDenied bounded).\nalice$ nd invoke d5223e85a22005ae70ca83fac51176397dd4e… 0 (record (n 101))\nhint lawDenied 41a17db6…: bounded: n over the bound\n\nrefused lawDenied\n\nexit refused · 44.7 ms · 12 frames · ticks 1,580 / 2,097,152 this window\ndemo generator: every step as expected, 0.3 s\nalice$ nd\nbob\n_\n×\nYou are bob, founder 1, member c3460b91…. Your keys stay in this tab. Your follow (your copy of the World) checks each command before your key signs it.\nCommands: create · write OBJ SLOT TEXT · read OBJ [?] · grant OBJ MEMBER RIGHTS · invoke OBJ N ARGS · install TEXT · sync\n\nbob$ nd\nTour\n_\n×\n\nOne World, two members (alice, bob), all in this tab. Type into their terminals, or press Run on each step.\n\nalice creates a cell: an object with numbered slots and no code. She owns it.\nalice writes slot 0. Her copy of the World checks the write before her key signs it. If the check fails, nothing is signed.\nalice reads the description of the cell. Click any id to open the object.\nalice grants bob the right to write the cell (mutate). The grant is a cell with its own id.\nbob writes slot 0 through the grant. His call names the state of the cell it expects (a pin). alice writes slot 0 while his signed call is in transit, so the writer declines his call (stale).\nThe writer lies: it changes one byte of every event it serves. bob's follow resets to genesis and replays the log. It checks each Turn and refuses the altered one (eventMismatch).\nA generator: a package whose method installs another package. The generated package has the law n <= 100; setting n = 101 is refused (lawDenied).\nThe meter: each Turn records its member and its ticks (evaluator steps). bob repeats an expensive call until his ticks for the window run out (ticksBudget).\nA time lock: a second World (A) runs in this tab. alice's lock releases only with a receipt showing that A admitted a call at or after the deadline height.\n\nMore: the Writer menu in the World window turns on each lie the conformance rows test, and runs its scene. Or try: write as bob without --via; install a package twice; New World.\n\nDemos\n_\n×\nDocument section with a hole Run\n14 commands\nGenerator: a package that installs a package Run\n7 commands\nMeter: ticks per member Run\n3 commands\nTime lock on another World's height Run\n17 commands\n\nEach demo types ordinary nd commands into the terminals, on the current World.\n\nObject 2beb1ef2…\n_\n×\nsource\talice's follow: read 2beb1ef2… ?\nupdated\tafter every command\nobject\t2beb1ef2…\nowner\talice:1e4aabca…\npackage\tc50f4d00…\ndoc\t\"installs a n-bounded record at the bound its argument names\"\nstate\t(rec)\ncore\t\n2489 bytes (the package code invoke runs)\n\nmethod 0\tgenerate (rec (max nat)) invoke…\ncall\t0 0 (sum (install (rec (pkg bytes))))\nstate\n\t(record)\nTerms\nObject d5223e85…\n_\n×\nsource\talice's follow: read d5223e85… ?\nupdated\tafter every command\nobject\td5223e85…\nowner\talice:1e4aabca…\npackage\t41a17db6…\nstate\t(rec (n nat))\ncore\t\n1442 bytes (the package code invoke runs)\n\nmethod 0\tset (rec (n nat)) invoke…\nlaw\tbounded\nstate\n\t(record (n 50))\nTerms\nRefusal\n×\n×\nrefused lawDenied\nhint lawDenied 41a17db610e5fafa485b3a7912e458d6fa80ac36e34152e8a5cbd8b511082854: bounded: n over the bound\ncommand\talice: nd invoke\nexit\trefused\nwriter's reply\tnothing: your follow refused the call before signing, so nothing was sent\n\nlawDenied: a law of the object refused the change. A law compares the old state with the new state.\n\nOK\n◆ nanodregg\nWorld\nFrames\nalice\nbob\nTour\nDemos\nObject 2beb1ef2…\nObject d5223e85…\nwriter: honest · 127 frames · 7 commands"
