{"forkText":"Hosted World\n_\n×\nrelay\twss://nano.demo.dregg.online/ws\norigin\t300868a61428ae94e8f407f99b519f716841afaea20921c9ec1ffcd54da15786\nsponsor\te3c57f4ff4fac8bc15f9be86c2082593be4c70dbb8546900c9cbe1c0ae0d56c9 (guest-book)\nyou\tmember fa9cc452afed1a79cdce0cbeacfc038d53668ce821c2da237c135acbca3a63e1 grant 7aac4f9b540aa0e2d61983b5654d1de09dafb6031d5c846c1aca255f6f363b5e\n\nThe writer is a host serve process on another machine. This tab holds your keys and your follow. The follow checks each step before your key signs. A second tab of this page is a second member.\n\nTerms\nrelay\nForwards frames between this tab and the writer. It is not trusted.\nguest-book\nThe member that enrols new members.\nsponsor\nThe member whose key signed the invitation.\nfollow\nYour own copy of the World. It replays the log and checks every entry.\nRelay\nThe relay \nis honest\nalters an event in the log\ndrops the last event of each log page\nloses the reply, then reports the call refused\nreports a cancel it never received\nserves a cancel alice did not sign\ndrops the call (a loss, not a lie)\n reset follow (cold)\nThe relay forwards every frame unchanged. Your follow checks every reply in any case.\nExample: choose \"alters an event in the log\", press reset follow, run nd sync. The writer logged the true Turn. Your follow checks the altered copy and refuses it (eventMismatch).\nFork check\n Check attestation\nTwo writers can serve the same genesis. A follow checks only its own writer. A signed head (attestation) from the other writer shows a fork: refused forkedWorld.\nLocal World","terminal":"you\n_\n×\nYou are you, founder 0, member fa9cc452…. Your keys stay in this tab. Your follow (your copy of the World) checks each command before your key signs it.\nCommands: create · write OBJ SLOT TEXT · read OBJ [?] · grant OBJ MEMBER RIGHTS · invoke OBJ N ARGS · install TEXT · sync\n\nyou$ nd create\ntx c37d152cbeaad130a526105bb04be1aa9632ada29a98b3cf347ac5867797a563\nid bd7187c4…\n\nexit ok · 489.0 ms · 11 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\nyou$ nd create\ntx fec96ca8c9b26ffaa3810bf7149464eb47f100ada51ddc90471e1a5d490adc0f\nid 7b471db7…\n\nexit ok · 366.8 ms · 11 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\nyou$ nd create\ntx bb46d94edefbfccb7c03bbfd1041d83e6478295130de37f9b91d2bf3adab24c8\nid ecda6f5a…\n\nexit ok · 399.2 ms · 11 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\nyou$ nd create\ntx caf1462243b6d674287294b7e01c0fab2282479f3d7dbfbeda865d6c2b596981\nid f4bd1da5…\n\nexit ok · 531.2 ms · 11 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\nyou$ nd create\ntx 3a0182e8f5625e9ecacceaa630e2b10e179ba75b5fa2275f71fba38bc5b758c9\nid c0fe0f72…\n\nexit ok · 420.5 ms · 11 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\nNo attestation from : Unexpected token '<', \"<!DOCTYPE \"... is not valid JSON\nAttestation from wss://nano.demo.dregg.online/ws: the other writer's head, signed by its guest-book. Your follow resets, replays your writer's log up to that position, and compares the two chains.\nyou$ nd sync --check c400000020000000300868a61428ae94e8f40…   (attestation from another writer)\nshared 12 e3c57f4f…\nheight 12\nchain 199b5dc7…\nroots 5ac26ef0…\n\nexit ok · 142.1 ms · 4 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\nyou$ nd","opts":[{"v":"honest","notes":"reset follow (cold)\nThe relay forwards every frame unchanged. Your follow checks every reply in any case.\nExample: choose \"alters an event in the log\", press reset follow, run nd sync. The writer logged the true Turn. Your follow checks the altered copy and refuses it (eventMismatch).\n"},{"v":"flipEvent","notes":"reset follow (cold)\nRelay: alters an event in the log. Conformance row audit (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 13, expects: refused eventMismatch. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back.\nExample: choose \"alters an event in the log\", press reset follow, run nd sync. The writer logged the true Turn. Your follow checks the altered copy and refuses it (eventMismatch).\n"},{"v":"dropLastEvent","notes":"reset follow (cold)\nRelay: drops the last event of each log page. Conformance row audit (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 14, expects: refused chainMismatch. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back.\nExample: choose \"alters an event in the log\", press reset follow, run nd sync. The writer logged the true Turn. Your follow checks the altered copy and refuses it (eventMismatch).\n"},{"v":"lieLookup","notes":"reset follow (cold)\nRelay: loses the reply, then reports the call refused. Conformance row settle (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 6, expects: ok. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back.\nExample: choose \"alters an event in the log\", press reset follow, run nd sync. The writer logged the true Turn. Your follow checks the altered copy and refuses it (eventMismatch).\n"},{"v":"lieCancel","notes":"reset follow (cold)\nRelay: reports a cancel it never received. Conformance row cancelLie (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 7, expects: hostContradicted cancelled open. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back.\nExample: choose \"alters an event in the log\", press reset follow, run nd sync. The writer logged the true Turn. Your follow checks the altered copy and refuses it (eventMismatch).\n"},{"v":"forgeCancel","notes":"reset follow (cold)\nRelay: serves a cancel alice did not sign. Conformance row cancelForged (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 8, expects: refused cancelForged. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back.\nExample: choose \"alters an event in the log\", press reset follow, run nd sync. The writer logged the true Turn. Your follow checks the altered copy and refuses it (eventMismatch).\n"},{"v":"neverForward","notes":"reset follow (cold)\nRelay: drops the call (a loss, not a lie). Conformance row rotate (a scripted test in Protocol.Rows), line 11, expects: open. Entries logged during the lie stay in the log after you switch back.\nExample: choose \"alters an event in the log\", press reset follow, run nd sync. The writer logged the true Turn. Your follow checks the altered copy and refuses it (eventMismatch).\n"}]}
