copy of the World) checks each command before your key signs it.\nCommands: create · write OBJ SLOT TEXT · read OBJ [?] · grant OBJ MEMBER RIGHTS · invoke OBJ N ARGS · install TEXT · sync\n\nWorld A is a second World in this tab, with its own writer. carol writes in A. The height of A is the clock.\ncarol$ nd create\ntx 9c5e1f85a323efc58bdc4c5c38aa3de206c9430f3b3dc02a2235153d8b06f6f8\nid d1e1ca58…\n\nexit ok · 31.7 ms · 11 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\ncarol$ nd write d1e1ca5859ab4556b4171e94629b1207fb51c… 0 tick\ntx a44c1a51ca1fc0a21bd19662ca2170de62bcc4a8810cd237b7aa92336daf0d12\n\nexit ok · 34.0 ms · 11 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\ncarol gets the receipt of that call: the head of A, and the height at which A admitted the call.\ncarol$ nd receipt 1f0b0ac0114f00bca067f3db2e9e6deff309c…\nreceipt 00020000…d11ba8ea…a21bd196…b7418def…0056651c…76200000…f8e36a70…4ac6ee70…70de62bc…6831f88c…5f05a0b2…00\nhead 2 2 bfe65468… b39782cb…\nsettle committed 2 1560d118…\n\nexit ok · 14.3 ms · 4 frames · ticks 0 / 2,097,152 this window\ncarol$ nd\nRefusal\n×\n×\nrefused eventMismatch\ncommand\tyou: nd sync\nexit\trefused\nwriter's reply\tnothing: your follow refused the call before signing, so nothing was sent\nlie on\trelay: alters an event in the log; lying frame #105 (log)\n\neventMismatch: an event on the log page does not match the Turn the writer admitted; one byte differs from what was signed. The follow refuses the page and keeps nothing from it.\n\nOK\n◆ nanodregg\nHosted World\nFrames\nyou\nTour\nDemos\ncarol (World A)\nwriter: LYING (flipEvent) · 107 frames · 13 commands"}
