{"bytesStart":"Object d5223e85…\n_\n×\nsource\talice's follow: read d5223e85… ?\nupdated\tafter every command\nobject\td5223e85…\nowner\talice:1e4aabca…\npackage\t41a17db6…\nstate\t(rec (n nat))\ncore\t\n1442 bytes (the package code invoke runs)\","links":[{"text":"d5223e85…","title":"d5223e85a22005ae70ca83fac51176397dd4e5002e0680caaadcfcb68b40bc7a"},{"text":"41a17db6…","title":"41a17db610e5fafa485b3a7912e458d6fa80ac36e34152e8a5cbd8b511082854"},{"text":"invoke…","title":""}],"sourceSections":"function openTerm(m, x, y) {\n  const out = $('div', { class: 'out sunken', 'aria-live': 'polite' });\n  const input = $('input', { class: 'sunken', 'aria-label': `${m.name}'s nd command`, placeholder: 'create   ·   write OBJ 0 hello   ·   read OBJ ?', autocomplete: 'off', spellcheck: 'false' });\n  const hist = []; let hi = 0;\n  input.addEventListener('keydown', async (e) => {\n    if (e.key === 'ArrowUp') { hi = Math.max(0, hi - 1); input.value = hist[hi] ?? ''; e.preventDefault(); }\n    if (e.key === 'ArrowDown') { hi = Math.min(hist.length, hi + 1); input.value = hist[hi] ?? ''; e.preventDefault(); }\n    if (e.key !== 'Enter' || !input.value.trim()) return;\n    const line = input.value.trim(); hist.push(line); hi = hist.length; input.value = '';\n    const argv = splitArgv(line.replace(/^nd\\s+/, ''));\n    await runIn(m, argv);\n  });\n  const body = $('div', { class: 'term' }, out, $('div', { class: 'line' }, $('span', { class: 'prompt' }, `${m.name}$ nd`), input));\n  terms.set(m.name, { out, m });\n  openWindow({ id: `term-${m.name}`, title: `${m.name}${m.world ? ` (World ${m.world})` : ''}`, x, y, w: 520, body });\n  print(m, $('span', { class: 'dim' }, `You are ${m.name}, founder ${m.index}${m.world ? ` of World ${m.world}` : ''}, member ${short(m.id)}. Your keys stay in this tab. Your follow (your copy of the World) checks each command before your key signs it.\\nCommands: create · write OBJ SLOT TEXT · read OBJ [?] · grant OBJ MEMBER RIGHTS · invoke OBJ N ARGS ·